                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Ed Pope: Gore 29.12.1799 at Lanesborough's / 19.1.1800 again / 21.1.1800 Goire at
                            John King's An Irish landed family, from Hist of Irish Parliament there
                            was John Gore 1735+-1814, Hon Richard Gore 1735/40 - 1807 (this one
                            perhaps the best candidate for dinner at King's as his estate was
                            hard-pressed), William Gore 1744-1815, and William Gore 1767-1832.
                            Edward Gore was custos brevium at £600 p.a. from 1782-1800. Francis Gore
                            was Lt Governor of Grenada 1791. Boyle's Court Guide of 1800 had Thomas
                            Gore 6 Queen St Mayfair / Miss Gore 17 Lower Brook St / Christopher Gore
                            Esq 20 Cumberland Place, Oxford St / Mrs Gore 1 Spanish Place,
                            Manchester Sq / Charles Gore Esq 6 Fitzroy St / Sir Booth Gore, Baronet,
                            9 Russell Place, Tottenmam Court Rd </p>
                    </note>
